@startuml OPS-Batch-Workflow
title Batch Workflow - Create, Submit, Approve, Reapprove and Cancel
hide empty description

start
:Authenticated user starts batch creation;
if (Coordinator or above,\nnot Admin, and on Delivery team?) then (yes)
else (no)
  :Reject with authorization error;
  stop
endif

:Validate batch data:\nunique batch ID; dates valid and start not past;\ntraining days > 0 and <= calendar days;\nhours within allowed limit; enrollments >= 1;\nat least one faculty member;
if (All validation passes and both approvers configured?) then (yes)
  :Resolve lookup references and assign approvers;
  :Assign creator as coordinator or sales SPOC when applicable;
  :Create batch with status\nApproval 1 Pending;
  :Send/log approval request notification;
else (no)
  :Return validation/configuration errors;\nDo not create batch;
  stop
endif

if (Submit or resubmit later?) then (yes)
  :Verify batch exists, caller has operational scope,\napprovers configured, and start date has not passed;
  if (Submission valid?) then (yes)
    :Assign configured approvers;\nreset both approval statuses to Pending;
    :Set status Approval 1 Pending;
  else (no)
    :Reject submission;
    stop
  endif
endif

if (Approver 1 decides?) then (Approve)
  :Verify caller is assigned approver 1\nand batch is Approval 1 Pending;
  :Set approver 1 status Approved\nand record approval timestamp;
  :Set status Approval 2 Pending;
else (Reject)
  :Verify caller is assigned approver 1\nand batch is Approval 1 Pending;
  :Set approver 1 status Rejected;\nrecord reason in remarks;
  :Set status Rejected;
  stop
endif

if (Approver 2 decides?) then (Approve)
  :Verify caller is assigned approver 2,\nlevel 1 approved, and status is Approval 2 Pending;
  :Set approver 2 status Approved\nand record approval timestamp;
  :Set approval reference and lock schema;
  if (Batch start date is in future?) then (yes)
    :Set status Upcoming;
  else (no)
    :Set status Ongoing;
  endif
else (Reject)
  :Verify caller is assigned approver 2,\nlevel 1 approved, and status is Approval 2 Pending;
  :Set approver 2 status Rejected;\nrecord reason in remarks;
  :Set status Rejected;
  stop
endif

:Batch is approved and in delivery lifecycle;
while (Batch not Completed or Cancelled?) is (yes)
  if (Qualifying business field changed?) then (yes)
    :Verify caller has operational scope;\nreject edits to Completed or Cancelled batches;
    :Record changed field before/after values\nin batch edit history;
    :Increment reapproval metadata;\nclear approval timestamps;\nreset both approvers to Pending;\nassign configured approvers;\nunlock schema;
    :Set status Approval 1 Pending;
    :Send/log reapproval request with changed fields;
    :Repeat level 1 then level 2 approval;
    if (Either approver rejects?) then (yes)
      :Set status Rejected;\nrecord rejection reason;
    else (no)
      :Set status Upcoming or Ongoing\naccording to start date;\nlock schema;
    endif
  else (no)
    if (Non-qualifying field edit?) then (yes)
      :Apply field-specific rules;\nremarks do not trigger reapproval;\nfinance fields require Finance team or Admin;
    endif
  endif

  if (Authorized lifecycle status change?) then (yes)
    :Require valid transition and reason;
    if (Target status needs approval\nbut both approvals are incomplete?) then (yes)
      :Keep/return batch to appropriate\napproval-pending status;
    else (no)
      :Record status-change audit entry\nin remarks and apply valid transition;
    endif
  endif

  if (Batch cancellation requested?) then (yes)
    :Verify coordinator-or-above role\nand operational scope;
    :Set batch status Cancelled;\nrecord reason and actor;
    :Cascade cancellation to all\nnon-terminal scheduled and logged sessions;
    stop
  endif

  if (Batch start date reached while Upcoming?) then (yes)
    :Set status Ongoing;
  endif
  if (Batch end date passed while Ongoing?) then (yes)
    :Set status Pending for Closure;
  endif

  if (Authorized batch closure succeeds?) then (yes)
    :Require all scheduled and logged sessions terminal\nand batch_avg_feedback not null;
    :Compute NPS or record NPS unavailable reason;
    :Set status Completed and lock schema;
    :Delete batch edit history transactionally;
    stop
  endif
endwhile (no)
stop

note right
Creation itself initializes status to Approval 1 Pending.
The submit endpoint can reassign configured approvers and reset
both approval decisions to Pending.

Reapproval-triggering fields include batch identity,
classification, client, delivery, schedule, enrollment,
ownership and faculty fields. Remarks and finance-only
fields do not trigger reapproval.

Schedule changes may be made while reapproval is pending;
they remain subject to batch date/session-count validation.
Manager/Admin direct approval is also available: Admin may
bypass approver checks; a Manager must satisfy level-1 approval.

Finance is a team, not a system role. Finance team
members may update finance fields even when schema-locked.

Cancellation is available before approval and from
Requested, Approval 1 Pending, Approval 2 Pending, Upcoming,
Ongoing, Pending for Closure and OnHold. It sets the batch
to Cancelled and cascades to all non-terminal sessions.
Cancelled is terminal.

Valid operational status transitions and OnHold/resume
rules are enforced by the lifecycle endpoint.
end note
@enduml
